~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
[EXPLAIN] What this step does
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
  Builds the two training sets from the raw table. Extreme potencies are those outside Q1 -
  1.5*IQR and Q3 + 1.5*IQR         (Tukey fences) of the pIC50 distribution. They are removed for
  the main analysis; a second set keeps them so the         pipeline can later measure how much
  they change the conclusions (sensitivity analysis, steps S01/S02/10).         Then structures
  that appear more than once (same canonical SMILES, different identifiers) are collapsed to one
  row,         because a duplicate in both the training and the test part of a fold would leak the
  answer.
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
